# LUXHUB sandbox (Spuerkeess, POST Luxembourg, Banque Raiffeisen, Banque de Luxembourg and the other banks in
# docs/luxhub.md). Copy to sandbox.env, which git ignores, and fill in.
#
# Not open to everyone: the bank APIs need an organisation account on https://developer.luxhub.com, which LUXHUB
# grants to authorised TPPs and to PSPs that have applied for a licence (form, then a registration code). A personal
# account sees only LUXHUB's own One Core API (checked 2026-10-21). Sign in through
# https://marketplace.luxhub.com/api/login/oauth2/auth/luxhub-sso: SIGN IN on developer.luxhub.com fails
# (?loginFailed=true).
#
# With an organisation account: Applications -> create one (PSD2, Sandbox, redirect URL below), subscribe it to
# the bank's "XS2A (Berlin Group)" API, then Authentication -> Generate new certificates. The client id and
# secret go below; the downloaded mock certificates are the mTLS client (QWAC-*.pem) and the signing key
# (QSealC-*.pem). Keep them in banks/luxhub/cert/ (ignored). Sandbox users: generic, any password, OTP 123456.

OBSDK_BANK=raiffeisenlu
OBSDK_COUNTRY=LU
OBSDK_ENV=sandbox

OBSDK_CLIENT_ID=
OBSDK_CLIENT_SECRET=
OBSDK_REDIRECT_URL=https://example.com/callback

OBSDK_TLS_CERT=banks/luxhub/cert/QWAC-cert.pem
OBSDK_TLS_KEY=banks/luxhub/cert/QWAC-key.pem
OBSDK_SEAL_KEY=banks/luxhub/cert/QSealC-key.pem
OBSDK_SEAL_CERT=banks/luxhub/cert/QSealC-cert.pem

OBSDK_PSU_IP=203.0.113.7
OBSDK_PSU_USER_AGENT=obdev/0.1
OBSDK_SESSION_FILE=banks/luxhub/sandbox.session.json
